From 5bb79786efccdf29e9c9d79749ba4694a37c7488 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:26:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Verifier V26: re-judge what custody accounts alone settle

In a custody season, V26:custody-state checks every Lot and Vault of the
program (post-states and the pinned slot) against the laws the custody
kernel checks before each write: a lot's conservation law and bounds,
its order and inbound slots, its state, HELD + expected <= QUOTA for an
open lot, STORES + CUSTODY_QUOTA <= CAP for a live vault, and, in the
pinned snapshot, a vault's counts against the open lots visible in it
(only "more visible than counted" is a FAIL: a missing account lowers the
visible sum, never raises it). A broken account is a FAIL
(CustodyLotBroken, CustodyOverCapacity, CustodyVaultCounts). A forfeited
lot or an open lot in a seized vault is UNVERIFIABLE
(CustodyRuleUndecided): forfeiture is not a decided rule.

The season itself is never a PASS: with no replay of the history every
custody trace stays CustodyUnverified. reserved <= held (needs the
current bell), the lot's address, signers and instruction order are not
judged. tests/custody_state.rs: the kernel's own writes (also 300 random
runs) never FAIL, twelve forged lots and a vault over CAP do, vault
counts fail only in the sound direction, undecided rules stay
UNVERIFIABLE, a broken post-state fails at its transaction.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
